---
// Quiz figure for Post 9: the same email field and Subscribe button drawn two ways.
---
<div class="qfig-uxq09sub">
  <svg viewBox="0 0 560 230" role="img" aria-label="Two email sign-up rows. Mock 1: the Subscribe button sits to the right of the input with a gap. Mock 2: the Subscribe button sits inside the input's border.">
    <text x="20" y="28" class="cap"><tspan data-lang-en>Mock 1</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>Mẫu 1</tspan></text>
    <rect x="20" y="40" width="380" height="44" rx="8" class="box" />
    <text x="38" y="67" class="ph">you@company.com</text>
    <rect x="412" y="40" width="128" height="44" rx="8" class="btn" />
    <text x="476" y="67" text-anchor="middle" class="bt"><tspan data-lang-en>Subscribe</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>Đăng ký</tspan></text>

    <text x="20" y="138" class="cap"><tspan data-lang-en>Mock 2</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>Mẫu 2</tspan></text>
    <rect x="20" y="150" width="520" height="44" rx="8" class="box" />
    <text x="38" y="177" class="ph">you@company.com</text>
    <rect x="416" y="156" width="118" height="32" rx="6" class="btn" />
    <text x="475" y="177" text-anchor="middle" class="bt"><tspan data-lang-en>Subscribe</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>Đăng ký</tspan></text>
  </svg>
</div>

<style>
  .qfig-uxq09sub { margin: 0; width: 100%; }
  .qfig-uxq09sub svg { display: block; width: 100%; min-width: 320px; height: auto; }
  .qfig-uxq09sub text { fill: var(--text-body); font-size: 14px; }
  .qfig-uxq09sub .cap { fill: var(--text); font-size: 14px; font-weight: 700; }
  .qfig-uxq09sub .ph { fill: var(--text-muted); font-size: 14px; }
  .qfig-uxq09sub .bt { fill: var(--bg); font-size: 14px; font-weight: 700; }
  .qfig-uxq09sub .box { fill: var(--bg); stroke: var(--border); stroke-width: 1.5; }
  .qfig-uxq09sub .btn { fill: var(--act-3); }
</style>
